From e7a63bf33dac3e302504d3541816a81b33536ecd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuanyuan Chen <cyyever@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 06:05:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hipGraph: reuse kernel-argument slots across exec updates

Every hipGraphExecUpdate / hipGraphExec*SetParams re-captures the node's
packet and bump-allocates a fresh kernel-argument slot; nothing is
reclaimed until the exec is destroyed. An exec updated once per launch
(per generated token in LLM serving) therefore grows device memory
without bound and eventually exhausts it (#10713, the trigger for
#10021).

Track the slots each node's packets use. When an update commits, the
node's previous slots are retired with the epoch of the last submitted
launch; each launch takes an epoch in Run and returns it from its
completion callback, and a retired slot is reused once no launch up to
its epoch is in flight, even while later launches keep the exec busy.
A same-device launch that fails partway drains its streams before the
callback runs. A failed capture or update discards the new slots and
keeps the old ones. Free slots are kept in a (device, size)-ordered
multimap for best-fit reuse.

Also register the hipGraphExecUpdate cases added by this series in the
hip-tests YAML config, which HIP_TEST_CASE requires.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
